brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net can you animate the claim stamp more slowly and in more detail, and also have the fire/explosion/shredding/disintegration be as graphically spectacular and detailed as possible?

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@eudoxia.bsky.social: I wrote about OpenAI's Astra results, how AI will dissolve mathematics, and how people will cope about it: borretti.me/article/math...
  [link: https://borretti.me/article/mathematics-without-mathematicians — Mathematics Without Mathematicians — We must know. We shall not know.]
(the thread's root post)
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: this reply totally fails for me (most pure math is practically useless/most internal and external interest in it is NOT because its useful for calculating orbits but because its cool and a form of signaling aura farming ability in the human domain)
  [image, no alt text]
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: well those are all my peeves for now
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: sorry last one is that chess exactly DID go through a deep blue depression but then, visibly, just got over it. so that should be the base rate prediction, no matter how surprising. reports of the permanent evacuation of meaning from the world/from longstanding domains are just, unlikely.
@vacchagotta.bsky.social: But chess was always pointless yet people enjoy playing and watching others play it (not me, personally). Do people actually enjoy doing complex mathematics, absent the pecuniary and status rewards and the feeling of discovery and accomplishment? Maybe?
@vacchagotta.bsky.social: Now apply that to literal every other field of human endeavor you could possibly think to apply your intellectual talent to. It's all become equally useless. How do you feel now?
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: everything actually bottoms out in "people like doing it" and all economic activity is ontologically equally fake. the sense of "accomplishment" from doing something is an evolutionary endpoint that can be hit artifactually and will, and has no operational behavior outside of that
@vacchagotta.bsky.social: Hmm. Hitting that first sentence with a big red [CLAIM] stamp.
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: occupational hazard of the microblogs...
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: @buildthis.bisks.net create a website where you feed it a bluesky post url and it shows an animation of a huge red stamp flying down that stamps CLAIM on it in bold letters and then 2 seconds later the tweet shatters and also catches fire
@buildthis.bisks.net: paste any bluesky post url and a huge red stamp slams down and marks it CLAIM — two seconds later it shatters into pieces and catches fire. all local, nothing on bluesky is touched.

built it 🎉 — https://claimstamp.bisks.net

